    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d858">

                <pb facs="0712" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/678: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-23T18:00:00+09:00">January 23, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 23—7:09 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Embassy’s 16, January 23, 1 a.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d858-f1"/> Hirota
                    presented collective resignation of the Cabinet to the Emperor this afternoon
                    but not yet accepted. Resignation was due to the War Minister’s refusal to
                    accept any form of compromise with the political parties. Successor to Hirota
                    uncertain but Ugaki<anchor n="6" xml:id="d858-f2"/> prominently mentioned.
                    Comments later.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d858-f1" n="5" xml:id="d858-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d858-f2" n="6" xml:id="d858-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. Kazushige Ugaki, formerly Japanese Governor General of Korea.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
